From: SacredTrees <121399723+SacredTrees@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 07:43:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] JavaScriptCore: property shape tables, getters, strings and
 loop doubles in the 68k template JIT

- get_by_id: each site gets a four-entry structure table after the
  code, filled after the slow path (fillGetByIdTable). An entry holds an
  own value, a getter (own, or on the prototype while the prototype keeps
  its structure; called as op_call calls, with a frame below this one)
  or a missing property (undefined while the prototype, the last on the
  chain, keeps its structure). At the end of a garbage collection,
  M68KTemplateJIT::reconcileCaches (from
  CodeBlock::reconcileLLIntInlineCachesAtGCEnd) clears the entries whose
  structures died. The prototype-load and unset cache modes run out of
  line instead of in the template.
- Strings: s[i] on a flat string (out of line, after the array path)
  gives the single-character string for codes below 256; .length of
  flat strings and ropes; String.prototype.charCodeAt at call sites whose
  call link holds it, checked at run time by its native function. VM.cpp
  keeps charCodeAt's intrinsic on C_LOOP M68K so the call site can see
  it.
- Loop register copies keep doubles in fp2-fp6: slots computed from a
  double constant or another double. Every write still goes to the
  frame, boxed; a double that an int-only instruction also uses stays in
  the frame only.
- op_check_traps gets a plain fast path.

The AmigaChrome Team.
